%erg 0.1
Title: pi-subagent-link no-ops on an npm-global Pi install
Created: 2026-10-12
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-12T13:54Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context
On host doudou, `~/.pi/agent/extensions/` holds only `idh-guard.ts` and
`~/.pi/agent/agents/` does not exist. `bash scripts/pi-subagent-link` prints
`no Pi install at ~/.pi/agent; nothing to link` and EXITS 0 while
linking nothing: it resolves the release from `~/.pi/agent/install/current-version`,
a layout that does not exist for an npm-global install (`~/.local/bin/pi` ->
`~/.local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`, v1.1.0). The
subagent door was verified on padme only (`skills/route/routes.json`,
2026-10-09).

Consequence: a Pi orchestrator on such a host silently loses the subagent door
and falls back to detached seats, with no signal that the link never happened.

## Fix shape
Resolve the install from the real path of the `pi` executable as a fallback,
and fail loudly (non-zero) rather than exit 0 when neither layout exists.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `scripts/pi-subagent-link` links the subagent extension and agents on an npm-global install (fixture: `pi` symlink into a `node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` tree)
- [ ] With neither layout present it exits non-zero with a message naming both paths it tried
- [ ] The existing `current-version` layout still works (regression test)

## Raid 1089 — Imagine (2026-10-14)

Proceed; the current host's managed Pi 1.2.0 does not invalidate the original
npm-global fixture. Preserve all three exit criteria. Keep managed release
lookup first; fall back through the actual PATH executable, real symlink target
and ancestor package root. Validate both index.ts and agents.ts modules before
linking. Do not hardcode either executable bin directory or create ~/bin.
Both-source failure names marker/release and the executable attempt; a broken
managed source may still fall back. No new dependency or generalized installer.

Author clarification: no ~/bin directory in the home; prefer ~/.local/bin for
Pi's public launcher. Requested upstream report deposited as
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/issues/10932, with selector reproduction.
It is auto-closed by the upstream new-contributor policy, awaiting maintainer
review. The installer can select even an absent ~/bin from PATH and later
create it. The harness helper will only create its extension destination.

Blind-spot pass: standalone helper tests would miss pi-haiku's stderr masking.
Smallest repair removes the stderr discard, preserving the wrapper's existing
continue-on-setup-failure behavior and Pi's exit status. Test the diagnostic
through that caller with synthetic fixtures; do not read real credential files.
The modules linked by this helper are index.ts and agents.ts, not user-specific
model-pinned agent definitions. No other material omission.

Estimated scope: two shell files, one focused subprocess test module and this
ticket; no registry collisions or monster-ticket signals. Implementation is
bounded; review/gates dominate elapsed time. Harness work is the deliverable.
